From: Tarik Caramanico <tarikcaramanico@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: bound native call redirection to the 32-bit table size

Backport upstream FEX commits:
  4dbb046d62c57639fd93d433bb64896df7332ff0
  3a2b1c0b438fed5062bebff0c5f7c8e21879fe48

NtDllRedirectionLUTSize is uint32_t. A 64-bit load includes the adjacent
four bytes in the bound, and the valid offsets exclude the size itself.
Load the declared width and reject offsets greater than or equal to it.

An isolated process calling the runtime's actual CheckCall routine with
controlled table entries gives 2 pass / 2 fail before, 4 / 0 after in both
validation modes. The probe restores all original runtime variables
before returning to x64 code. This does not establish game compatibility.

diff --git a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S
index 754511c..8ed5976 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S
@@ -163,9 +163,9 @@ DIRECT_SYSCALL_WRAPPER("#NtProtectVirtualMemoryNative", WineNtProtectVirtualMemo
   subs x16, x11, x9
   b.lo end
   adrp x17, NtDllRedirectionLUTSize
-  ldr x17, [x17, #:lo12:NtDllRedirectionLUTSize]
+  ldr w17, [x17, #:lo12:NtDllRedirectionLUTSize]
   cmp x16, x17
-  b.hi end
+  b.hs end
   adrp x17, NtDllRedirectionLUT
   ldr x17, [x17, #:lo12:NtDllRedirectionLUT]
   ldr w11, [x17, x16, lsl #2]
